Falsifies `system_tests::user::map_revocation_window_tests::a_destroy_inside_a_memory_region_map_leaves_no_mapping`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the tree as it stood until 2026-10-04 (UTC): the patch puts `MemoryRegion::MAP` back
to retyping and mapping its page first, then taking the mapping registry only to record it, with
the seam between. `MemoryRegion::DESTROY` held at the seam claims the region, scans a log the
mapping is not yet in, and hands the page back; the mapping is recorded after it, alive, over a
page the allocator owns again: the use-after-free §13 (capability revocation and untyped
reclamation) exists to prevent.

This was the live tree. It was not recorded anywhere before this lane; the map-revocation-window
lane found it by asking which other mapping paths read their source outside the record's hold.

Expected to fail: `assert!(!REPORT.mapped.load(..), "a MemoryRegion::MAP held while its region was destroyed kept its mapping ...")`.
Confirmed red on riscv64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC) against the fixed tree, at
`map_revocation_window_tests.rs:407`, the assertion predicted.

**The assertions above the headline stay green under this patch**: the seam was reached, the
neighbouring page that builds the tables mapped, and the region no longer resolves.

Nothing here is architecture-specific, so one patch serves every leg.

**Re-cut on 2026-10-05 (UTC) by the page-tables-outlive-destroy lane**, because `memory_region_map`
now retypes its leaf itself and its tables through the hold (`MappingHold::retype_table`), so the
old hunk no longer applied. The defect is the same: the page is retyped and mapped in one hold of
the registry and recorded in another, with the seam between. Replayed red on aarch64 against the
re-cut, at the headline assertion.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/memory_region.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/memory_region.rs
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/memory_region.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/memory_region.rs
@@ -74,8 +74,6 @@
     if !paging::is_user_page_va::<crate::arch::mmu::Format>(va) {
         return Err(Error::BadPointer);
     }
-    #[cfg(feature = "system_tests")]
-    crate::delegation_pause::here(); // no lock held
     let mut hold = crate::revoke::hold();
     let root = mmu::current_user_root();
     // The leaf's page, then its record, then the tables, each table recorded as it is retyped:
@@ -88,20 +86,26 @@
     // revocation and untyped reclamation)). No capability names the page, and it is fresh, so the
     // record's writable-and-executable check finds nothing to refuse.
     let flags = paging::Flags::user_data();
-    let recorded = hold
-        .record_mapping(phys, root, va, flags, crate::revoke::PageMapSource::NoCapability)
-        .map_err(|_| Error::OutOfMemory)?;
-    match mmu::map_current_user_page_frame(va, phys, flags, || {
+    let mapped = mmu::map_current_user_page_frame(va, phys, flags, || {
         hold.retype_table(region, root, va)
-    }) {
-        Ok(()) => Ok(0),
-        Err(e) => {
-            hold.forget_recorded(root, recorded);
-            Err(match e {
-                paging::MapError::OutOfPageFrames => Error::OutOfMemory,
-                _ => Error::BadPointer, // misaligned, already mapped, or wrong half
-            })
+    });
+    drop(hold);
+    #[cfg(feature = "system_tests")]
+    crate::delegation_pause::here(); // no lock held
+    let mut hold = crate::revoke::hold();
+    match mapped {
+        Ok(()) => {
+            if hold
+                .record_mapping(phys, root, va, flags, crate::revoke::PageMapSource::NoCapability)
+                .is_err()
+            {
+                mmu::unmap_user_at(root, va);
+                return Err(Error::OutOfMemory);
+            }
+            Ok(0)
         }
+        Err(paging::MapError::OutOfPageFrames) => Err(Error::OutOfMemory),
+        Err(_) => Err(Error::BadPointer), // misaligned, already mapped, or wrong half
     }
